      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJEFFREY B. WALL, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nEDWIN S. KNEEDLER, Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Federal Respondents.\nJOSHUA A. KLEIN, Deputy Solicitor General, Oakland, California; on behalf of the State Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The EPA waiver here allows California to limit the number of vehicles that run on liquid fuel. Petitioners make and sell liquid fuel, so vacating the -- waiver would redress their injuries in two ways."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Wall, taking a step away -- back from the evidence you just provided or the points you just made, what is your rule? How would you articulate -- articulate your categorical rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Diamond Alternative Energy, LLC (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our rule is that when the government denies a party the ability to compete in a marketplace the -- and the party sues to have that market restriction lifted, there is redressability because the party is asking for the thing to be taken away that's causing its injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What you want then is an advisory opinion. And at a certain point, we move from giving -- giving you relief or not, but that's not this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But isn't that a tell here? I mean, EPA, as you, of course, know, routinely raises standing objections when there's even -- even a hint of a question about it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the D.C. Circuit rejected, and they haven't sought review of that here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "would have been required to say, if this waiver is set aside, I will engage in the conduct that the regulation prohibits, which is producing a fleet that doesn't comply with the California measures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Federal courts don't assume there's standing. The presumption runs the other way. The party who brings a case must establish that it, in fact, meets each element of standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State Respondents",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners failed their burden to establish a non-speculative likelihood that automakers would sell more gas cars, and Petitioners sell more fuel, without the waiver."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Okay. Well, let's just take the trucks then. Let's take the light trucks. Are you willing to say that without your rules, the light truck industry would continue marketing the mix of vehicles it's currently marketing or manufacturing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Klein",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners' declarations as to remedy were entirely speculative and -- sorry, not speculative. Conclusory, right? They just said this would be redressed if you strike down the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could you go back to the very first question that Justice Thomas asked you: Why do you need the waiver at this point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just a few points, Your Honor. The first, Mr. Kneedler says, look, who knows what will happen in the market five, 10 years down the road. Just so, that's why the Court should adopt our front-line rule. We should be allowed to compete in this marketplace because we don't know exactly what will happen down the road."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-7",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05f2a4cd4aa661bb34fc5eed40dbcedbaee6f16ba85e0d323d6e65ffb6ea0a0d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05f2a4cd4aa6-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
